bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_input_button_percent_width_ignored_2026-11-28, 0, "<div><input type=submit value=Go style=width:50%><button>HTML</button></div> in a 400 px body: Chrome 159 sizes the input 250 px (border columns 0 199 253 at k=1 with the 1px #94a3b8 border; 0 796 1013 at k=4) and its label ink sits at 92..107. Simple (base 2bc96bcf7de and lane) paints an 8 px box (borders 0 8 63 at k=1, 0 32 249 at k=4) with no label ink: the percentage-width sentinel (width_px < 0) is not resolved for an input button. Also, after <button style=width:30%>Go</button> an <input type=button value='CSS Paint'> ends one column early (k=1 198 vs Chrome 199, k=4 793 vs 794)."

